<title>DENMARK: Danish March consumer confidence +9 (Feb +8).</title>
<headline>Danish March consumer confidence +9 (Feb +8).</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's consumer confidence indicator was +9 in March 1997, up from +8 in February, the National Statistics Office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>		   March 97	    Feb 97	   March 96</p>
<p>		    +9		     +8		   +5</p>
<p>NOTE: The survey asks a cross section of Denmark's population its views on current personal and national economic trends, along with consumer intentions for coming months. Changes in consumer confidence are indicated by a higher or lower weighted rating, rather than by index. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969650</p>
</text>
